<section id="personal-copy" aria-labelledby="copy-title">
<h2 id="copy-title">Create an editable personal itinerary</h2>
<p>The itinerary’s two movement legs become a private My Route. Local days, weather allowance and research tasks become editable trip notes. A personal copy retains the template version and source snapshot; later editorial updates do not overwrite your work.</p>
<div class="bh-table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Transfer details"><table><caption>What the personal copy contains</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Transferred</th><th scope="col">What you must supply or review</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><th scope="row">Two named destination references</th><td>Actual departure/arrival choices, their coordinate limitations and the complete approach paths</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Two movement legs with editable owner-supplied distance estimates</th><td>Review or replace each leg’s mileage and its source or calculation method for your trip. Measurement method, chart source and date are unspecified.</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Explicit performance inputs</th><td>Speed in knots, total underway US gal/h, daily hours, usable fuel and allowances</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">#bhWorksheet.reserve_pct#% added reserve mode</th><td>Review the reserve policy; no additional percentage is subtracted from tank capacity</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Local/weather days and research notes</th><td>Edit the notes and trip expectations as your plan changes; these are not scheduled laydays</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<cfif bhPublished>
<div class="bh-actions"><a class="bh-button" href="#bhBase#/app/join.cfm" data-fpw-auth-intent="planner" data-fpw-guide-template="#encodeForHTMLAttribute(bhManifest.template_key)#" data-fpw-guide-version="#bhManifest.template_version#" data-fpw-auth-source-page="bahamas_guide" data-fpw-auth-section="worked_itinerary" data-fpw-auth-cta-type="plan_trip" data-fpw-auth-label="Use this itinerary">Use this itinerary</a></div>
<p class="bh-meta">Creates an editable personal copy after sign-in or registration. Ordinary repeat selections reopen your current copy of this version. Use the planner’s explicit Create another copy action for an additional copy.</p>
<cfelse>
<div class="bh-note"><p><strong>Personal-copy import is not released yet.</strong> Source semantics have been recorded, including Brown’s Marina’s unstated coordinate datum. Local workflow checks have been completed. Publication awaits owner review and the separate production checks.</p><p>Review the example here while the import remains unavailable. No account is required to read or print it.</p></div>
</cfif>
<p>Changing a copied distance clears that leg’s active source/method and prior review. The new value is a <strong>Member-entered estimate</strong>; the original estimate remains in the import snapshot. Enter a source or method and review the changed leg before creating a Float Plan.</p>
<p><strong>Save planning draft</strong> keeps unfinished work, including missing source/method, null mileage and notes. Complete calculation inputs are required for a normal saved-trip snapshot. Every movement leg must then be explicitly confirmed or replaced by the member before entering the Float Plan workflow. Confirmation records the member’s review; it never labels the route independently verified.</p>
</section>
<section id="stops" aria-labelledby="stops-title">
<h2 id="stops-title">Know what each point represents</h2>
<figure class="bh-map"><p class="bh-map-help">On a narrow screen, scroll the map horizontally. <a href="#bhAsset#bimini-context.svg">Open the full port everglades and bimini reference map</a>. The table below provides the same locations.</p><div class="bh-map-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Port Everglades and Bimini reference map; scroll horizontally if needed"><img src="#bhAsset#bimini-context.svg" width="1000" height="560" alt="Numbered Port Everglades and Bimini destination-reference map with a dashed schematic connection. The stop table describes both points, coordinate sources and limitations."></div><figcaption>Dashed connection = schematic relationship only. It supplies no navigable approach geometry, depth, clearance or distance. Coastlines use Natural Earth context data. The source and role of each actual template reference are listed below.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="bh-table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Template stop references"><table><caption>Template destination references — version #bhManifest.template_version#</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stop</th><th scope="col">Published coordinates &amp; role</th><th scope="col">Source and review task</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<cfset bhStopNumber = 0>
<cfloop array="#bhManifest.stops#" index="bhStop">
<cfset bhStopNumber = bhStopNumber + 1>
<tr><th scope="row">#bhStopNumber# · #encodeForHTML(bhStop.name)#</th><td><cfif structKeyExists(bhStop,'original_coordinate_text')>#encodeForHTML(bhStop.original_coordinate_text)#<cfelse>Reference pending</cfif><small>#encodeForHTML(replace(bhStop.coordinate_role,'_',' ','all'))#. Datum: #encodeForHTML(replace(bhStop.datum,'_',' ','all'))#.</small></td>
<td><cfloop array="#bhStop.source_ids#" index="bhId">#bhSource(bhId,bhSources[bhId].authority)# </cfloop>
<cfif bhStop.key EQ 'bimini'><small>Brown’s is a candidate destination, not a berth reservation or offshore approach waypoint. The source does not state coordinate datum or revision. Ask the marina about current approach conditions and review the intended path.</small>
<cfelse><small>Rounded NOAA reference published November 1, 2026; it replaces the earlier, more precise Light List value. This is not a berth or anchorage. Check current notices and review staging/harbor movements separately.</small></cfif></td></tr>
</cfloop></tbody></table></div>
<p>The selected Bimini candidate is <strong>Brown’s Marina</strong>, based on its first-party published location. This replaces the earlier Big Game Club berth candidate in this example. Brown’s page describes changing harbor sandbars and directs visitors to contact the marina. A published marina location does not validate the harbor approach.</p>
<div class="bh-table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Actual template mileage"><table><caption>Example route distance — review for your trip.</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Leg</th><th scope="col">Planning mileage</th><th scope="col">Source/method and review</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<cfloop array="#bhManifest.legs#" index="bhLeg"><tr><th scope="row">#encodeForHTML(bhLeg.key EQ 'outbound' ? '1 → 2 · Outbound: Port Everglades → Brown’s Marina' : '2 → 1 · Return: Brown’s Marina → Port Everglades')#</th><td><cfif isNull(bhLeg.distance_nm)>Unset<cfelse>#bhOne(bhLeg.distance_nm)# NM estimate</cfif><small>#encodeForHTML(replace(bhLeg.distance_kind,'_',' ','all'))#</small></td><td>#encodeForHTML(bhLeg.distance_method)#<small>Member review: not yet recorded. Geometry: schematic.</small></td></tr></cfloop>
</tbody></table></div>
<div class="bh-note"><p><strong><cfif bhTemplateMissingLegs>Known-leg subtotal: #bhOne(bhTemplateDistance)# NM — incomplete.<cfelse>Example route distance total: #bhOne(bhTemplateDistance)# NM — review for your trip.</cfif></strong> The distances are owner-supplied planning estimates, not independently verified route lengths. The return uses the same example path in reverse. Measurement method, chart source and date are unspecified. Each leg still requires member review.</p><p>Your personal copy requires explicit speed and fuel-burn inputs before it can show complete time and fuel estimates. <cfif bhTemplateMissingLegs EQ 0>At the worksheet’s illustrative #bhWorksheet.planning_speed_kn# kn and #bhWorksheet.underway_burn_us_gph# US gal/h, these #bhOne(bhTemplateDistance)# NM produce <strong>#bhTime(bhTemplateHours)#</strong>, <strong>#bhOne(bhTemplateBurn)# US gal</strong> base consumption and <strong>#bhOne(bhTemplateRequired)# US gal</strong> including #bhWorksheet.reserve_pct#% added reserve. These operating assumptions are not prefilled or confirmed for your boat.<cfelse>Missing mileage prevents a complete-trip time or fuel estimate.</cfif></p></div>
<p>#bhSource("S8","Big Game Club’s 47.6 nm published approach comparison")# describes different references and links to a chart dated 2009. It is neither a current berth-to-berth validation nor a distance for the PE buoy–Brown’s Marina pair. It stays separate from both the imported legs and the illustrative worksheet.</p>
</section>
<section id="enter-mileage" aria-labelledby="mileage-title">
<h2 id="mileage-title">Review mileage for the route you intend to travel</h2>
<p>New personal copies start with #bhOne(bhManifest.legs[1].distance_nm)# NM outbound and #bhOne(bhManifest.legs[2].distance_nm)# NM return, labeled “Example route distance — review for your trip.” These owner-supplied estimates have no documented measurement method, chart source or measurement date. Review or replace them using the steps below once this itinerary is released. A straight line between the reference points, the marina’s Miami distance and the separate 60 nm worksheet are not mileage sources for these legs.</p>
<ol class="bh-steps">
<li><strong>Define the movement.</strong> Check the planner’s endpoints against your intended departure and arrival. The PE buoy reference excludes travel from your Florida berth. Include any staging or harbor movements you add, and account for changed endpoints before measuring.</li>
<li><strong>Measure a reviewed water path.</strong> In current charting or route-planning tools, plot the passage and harbor approach your skipper intends to use. Check source dates, depth/draft constraints and local information. Record that tool’s route-distance result in nautical miles; do not measure this page’s dashed schematic line. FPW does not independently validate the plotted path.</li>
<li><strong>Review or replace one leg’s estimate.</strong> In <em>Review your planning estimates</em> → <em>Movement legs and member mileage review</em>, review the copied value or enter your replacement in <strong>Planning mileage estimate (nm)</strong>.</li>
<li><strong>Keep the provenance accurate.</strong> In <strong>Source or calculation method</strong>, retain the owner-supplied description if you keep the example estimate. If you replace it, record the basis you actually used: endpoints, chart/tool and edition or update date, measured route reference, measurement date and any allowance where known. Leave unknown details unspecified. Do not put a passenger’s personal information here.</li>
<li><strong>Review that leg.</strong> Select <strong>Confirm or replace this mileage</strong> after checking the value and method. Repeat independently for the return, including any changed approach. The recorded review does not make either route independently verified.</li>
<li><strong>Keep unfinished work honest.</strong> Leave unknown mileage blank and select <strong>Save planning draft</strong>. Known-leg totals remain incomplete. Reopen the draft from My Routes to continue; confirm explicit speed and consumption, complete required trip inputs, then use <strong>Save trip</strong>. Every movement leg needs a current member review before Float Plan creation.</li>
</ol>
<p>Changing an endpoint, mileage, method or geometry requires a fresh review of the affected leg. A member-created map line remains labeled member-created; a numeric mileage entry does not turn the schematic connection into a navigation track.</p>
</section>
<section id="worksheet" aria-labelledby="worksheet-title">
<h2 id="worksheet-title">Illustrative time and fuel worksheet</h2>
<p><strong>#encodeForHTML(bhWorksheet.label)#.</strong> This arithmetic example assumes #bhOne(bhWorksheet.legs[1].distance_nm)# nm for each movement. These distances are not sourced route lengths for the template’s endpoints.</p>
<div class="bh-grid"><div class="bh-panel"><h3>Explicit assumptions</h3><ul>
<li>Speed: <strong>#bhWorksheet.planning_speed_kn# kn</strong>; total-vessel underway consumption: <strong>#bhWorksheet.underway_burn_us_gph# US gal/h</strong>.</li>
<li>Nominal fuel aboard: 200 US gal; unusable: 10 US gal; usable aboard: <strong>#bhOne(bhWorksheet.usable_fuel_us_gal)# US gal</strong>.</li>
<li>Idle and auxiliary allowance: <strong>0 US gal</strong> in this illustration; add the actual allowance when applicable.</li>
<li>Reserve: <strong>#bhWorksheet.reserve_pct#% added to base consumption</strong>, applied once.</li>
<li>One knot is one nautical mile per hour. One nautical mile is 1,852 metres.</li>
</ul></div><div><h3>The calculation</h3><p>Movement time = planning distance ÷ speed.<br>Underway fuel = movement time × total-vessel consumption.<br>Reserve = base consumption × #bhWorksheet.reserve_pct#%.<br>Required quantity = base consumption + reserve.</p><p>Calculate at full precision, then display distance and fuel to one decimal and time to the nearest minute. These results are estimates and do not decide whether a crossing is safe.</p></div></div>
<div class="bh-table-wrap" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Illustrative movement calculation"><table><caption>Illustrative estimates — constructed worksheet assumptions</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Movement</th><th scope="col">Distance estimate</th><th scope="col">Time estimate</th><th scope="col">Fuel estimate</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<cfloop array="#bhWorksheet.legs#" index="bhWLeg"><tr><th scope="row">#encodeForHTML(bhWLeg.key EQ 'outbound' ? 'Outbound illustration' : 'Return illustration')#</th><td class="bh-number">#bhOne(bhWLeg.distance_nm)# nm</td><td class="bh-number">#bhTime(bhWLeg.distance_nm / bhWorksheet.planning_speed_kn)#</td><td class="bh-number">#bhOne(bhWLeg.distance_nm / bhWorksheet.planning_speed_kn * bhWorksheet.underway_burn_us_gph)# US gal</td></tr></cfloop>
<tr><th scope="row">Local days</th><td colspan="3">Notes only; no boat excursion or fuel consumption assumed</td></tr>
<tr><th scope="row">Movement total estimate</th><td class="bh-number">#bhOne(bhWDistance)# nm</td><td class="bh-number">#bhTime(bhWHours)#</td><td class="bh-number">#bhOne(bhWBurn)# US gal</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
<p>Reserve estimate: #bhOne(bhWBurn)# × #bhWorksheet.reserve_pct#% = <strong>#bhOne(bhWReserve)# US gal</strong>.<br>Estimated required departure quantity: #bhOne(bhWBurn)# + #bhOne(bhWReserve)# = <strong>#bhOne(bhWRequired)# US gal</strong>.<br>Usable fuel above that calculation: #bhOne(bhWorksheet.usable_fuel_us_gal)# − #bhOne(bhWRequired)# = <strong>#bhOne(bhWorksheet.usable_fuel_us_gal - bhWRequired)# US gal</strong>.</p>
<p>The percentage is not also subtracted from capacity. These results do not include a fuel-stop assumption or an assurance of range in actual conditions.</p>
<h3>A slower operating-point comparison</h3>
<p>Independently assume #bhWorksheet.slow_speed_kn# kn and #bhWorksheet.slow_burn_us_gph# US gal/h for the same #bhOne(bhWDistance)# illustrative nm. The resulting estimate is <strong>#bhTime(bhSlowHours)#</strong>, <strong>#bhOne(bhSlowBurn)# US gal</strong> base burn and <strong>#bhOne(bhSlowBurn * (1 + bhWorksheet.reserve_pct / 100))# US gal</strong> including reserve. The consumption rate is an assumption for that operating point, not a claim about the effect of slowing every boat.</p>
<figure class="bh-figure bh-figure--compact"><img src="#bhAsset#time-fuel-comparison.svg" width="560" height="620" loading="lazy" alt="Illustrative comparison: 20 knots at 18 US gallons per hour takes 6 hours and 129.6 US gallons including reserve; 7 knots at 4 US gallons per hour takes 17 hours 9 minutes and 82.3 US gallons."><figcaption>Same illustrative mileage; independently supplied performance assumptions. Separate time and fuel scales. The visible worksheet supplies the exact values and reserve method.</figcaption></figure>
</section>
<section id="flexible-days" aria-labelledby="days-title"><h2 id="days-title">Keep the timetable flexible</h2><p>These are planning notes, not scheduled laydays or a forecast. Two local days and two additional waiting days do not guarantee a workable weather window.</p>
<ol class="bh-timeline"><cfloop array="#bhManifest.days#" index="bhDay"><li class="#listFindNoCase('local,weather',bhDay.kind) ? 'bh-flex' : ''#"><strong>#encodeForHTML(bhDay.label)#</strong>#encodeForHTML(bhDay.description)#</li></cfloop></ol>
<p>Choose a departure date only after the route, vessel, crew, current forecast, arrival conditions and alternatives have been considered together. Use the <a href="#bhHub###florida-crossing">crossing source checklist</a> and <a href="#bhHub###entry-and-return">entry/return checklist</a>.</p>
</section>
<section id="changed-plan" aria-labelledby="changed-title"><h2 id="changed-title">When the plan changes</h2>
<div class="bh-grid"><div class="bh-panel"><h3>Return delayed and mileage revised</h3><p>The return is delayed two days. After reviewing the intended path, the member changes the return planning allowance from #bhOne(bhWorksheet.legs[2].distance_nm)# to #bhOne(bhWorksheet.revised_return_distance_nm)# nm and records the method. In this separate illustration:</p>
<ul><li>Movement distance estimate: <strong>#bhOne(bhChangedDistance)# nm</strong></li><li>Movement time estimate: <strong>#bhTime(bhChangedHours)#</strong></li><li>Base fuel estimate: <strong>#bhOne(bhChangedBurn)# US gal</strong></li><li>Estimated quantity including reserve: <strong>#bhOne(bhChangedBurn * (1 + bhWorksheet.reserve_pct / 100))# US gal</strong></li></ul>
<p>The changed leg’s previous review is invalid. Review it again. Reconsider accommodation, provisions, clearance validity, auxiliary fuel and shore-contact expectations.</p></div>
<div class="bh-panel"><h3>Return mileage has no defensible basis</h3><p>Leave it unset. If only the illustrative outbound #bhOne(bhWorksheet.legs[1].distance_nm)# nm is known, the display should say:</p><p class="bh-note"><strong>Known-leg subtotal: #bhOne(bhWorksheet.legs[1].distance_nm)# nm, #bhTime(bhWorksheet.legs[1].distance_nm / bhWorksheet.planning_speed_kn)#, #bhOne(bhWorksheet.legs[1].distance_nm / bhWorksheet.planning_speed_kn * bhWorksheet.underway_burn_us_gph)# US gal — incomplete; return mileage missing.</strong></p><p>Do not display a complete-trip fuel-sufficiency result. Saving and reopening the planning draft must preserve the missing value, source/method, notes and incomplete state.</p></div></div>
<h3>What invalidates a leg’s member review?</h3><p>An affected endpoint or coordinate change, distance or source/method change, geometry revision, or reorder that changes endpoint pairs requires a new review. Added legs start unreviewed. Member-plotted geometry remains labeled member-created; confirmation never turns a schematic line into independently verified navigation.</p>
</section>
<section id="review-tasks" aria-labelledby="review-title"><h2 id="review-title">Your review before the Float Plan workflow</h2>
<ul class="bh-checklist"><li>Confirm the exact endpoint pair and current approach information for every movement.</li><li>Review or replace each leg’s owner-supplied mileage and record its actual source or calculation method; leave unknown details unspecified.</li><li>Confirm speed in knots and total-vessel US gal/h, reserve mode, usable fuel and relevant allowances.</li><li>Explicitly confirm or replace every leg’s current mileage; review again after changes.</li><li>Review the complete saved snapshot, notes and schedule before progressing into Float Plan creation.</li><li>Confirm the shore contact understands changes, expected updates and the reporting plan.</li></ul>
<div class="bh-actions"><button type="button" class="bh-button bh-button--secondary" data-bh-print>Print this worked example</button><a href="#bhHub#" class="bh-button bh-button--secondary">Back to the Bahamas guide</a></div><p class="bh-meta">This is the public example’s print view. It contains no personal trip data, continuation tokens or private route identifiers. The planner’s separate planning summary preserves your own draft’s inputs and review state.</p>
</section>
<section id="sources" class="bh-sources" aria-labelledby="sources-title"><h2 id="sources-title">Sources, dates and limitations</h2><p>Retrieval confirms what a source says. It does not confirm navigation, current berthing or stock. Published coordinate datum and revision are retained where stated; missing metadata remains explicitly missing.</p>
<ul><cfloop array="#['S18','S10b','S10','S10a','S8','S9','S1','S3','S3a','S3b','S5','S5a','S5b','S6','S6a','S6b','S7','S16','S16a']#" index="bhId"><li>#bhSource(bhId,bhSources[bhId].authority & ' — ' & bhSources[bhId].topic)#<small>#encodeForHTML(bhSources[bhId].claim)# Accessed #encodeForHTML(bhSources[bhId].accessed_at)#. #encodeForHTML(bhSources[bhId].effective_date)#. Status: #encodeForHTML(replace(bhSources[bhId].verification_status,'_',' ','all'))#.</small></li></cfloop></ul>
</section>
